+### CPU-heads core
+
+`modeld` also takes a model with the same five inputs whose outputs are
+`out_hidden` [1, 512] and, per head, the last ReLU feature `hx_<head>`: the
+student distilled for this NPU in the separate supercombo_distill project. Each
+head's last linear layer runs on the CPU in fp32 (`src/model/cpu_heads.h`), so
+small values such as the plan's yaw keep their precision instead of going
+through a U16 output scale. The weights are a `<name>.heads` file next to
+`<name>.axmodel`; the outputs fill the same [2576] layout as the split core
+(`kCpuHeadParts` in `src/model/model_output_assembly.h`).
+
+```text
+hx_meta 64, hx_desire_pred 32, hx_pose 32, hx_wide_from_device 32,
+hx_road_transform 32, hx_lanes 64, hx_lane_prob 16, hx_road_edges 32,
+hx_lead 64, hx_lead_prob 16, hx_plan 256, hx_desire_state 32  (float)
+<name>.heads: "EPHEADS1", u32 head count, per head char name[32], u32 in,
+              u32 out, f32 W[out][in], f32 b[out]  (little-endian)
+```
+
+`modeld` refuses the model if the `.heads` file is missing, has another head,
+or any width differs from the axmodel's outputs or the layout. `EDGEPILOT_MODEL`
+selects it ([Runtime options](../docs/runtime-options.md)).
+
